setup:
Create a reduced full-ground playing area.
Divide players into two balanced teams.
Nominate a captain, defensive leader, midfield leader and forward leader for each team.
Give teams five minutes to establish:
starting structure;
defensive priority;
ball-movement plan;
stoppage roles;
interchange plan;
scoreboard-management principles.
The coach establishes safety rules, playing time and scoring only.
During play, the coach does not provide tactical instructions.

Create a reduced match-simulation field appropriate to the age and ability of the group.
Mark a scoring zone at each end.
Add optional side scoring gates, lanes and field thirds.
Divide players into two balanced teams.
Nominate player leaders.
Prepare assessment categories covering:
possession;
width and depth;
support;
movement after disposal;
scoring-zone use;
turnover reaction;
contested possession;
pressure;
defensive shape;
team ball movement;
tactical adaptability;
scoreboard management;
communication;
leadership.
Conduct five progressive phases.
Contact, field size and workload must be modified for younger, returning and Over 35 players.
